+import test from 'node:test';
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
+import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
+
+// Regression guard: the Tools page links to ../#troubleshooter and ../#health-score, but the
+// configurator only ever parsed #cfg= share links — so those "Open →" cards silently did
+// nothing. handleDeepLink() must map them to the real UI actions on load.
+
+const app = await readFile(new URL('../src/js/app.js', import.meta.url), 'utf8');
+
+test('handleDeepLink exists and is invoked once after initial render', () => {
+  assert.match(app, /function handleDeepLink\(hash\) \{/, 'handleDeepLink not defined');
+  assert.match(app, /try \{ handleDeepLink\(location\.hash\); \} catch/, 'handleDeepLink not called on load');
+});
+
+test('handleDeepLink maps the two Tools-page anchors and leaves #cfg= to the share-link path', () => {
+  assert.match(app, /if \(hash === '#troubleshooter'\) \{ setTimeout\(showTroubleshooter, 300\); return; \}/,
+    '#troubleshooter not mapped to showTroubleshooter()');
+  assert.match(app, /if \(hash === '#health-score'\) \{ step = STEPS; pushStep\(\); render\(\); window\.scrollTo\(0, 0\); return; \}/,
+    '#health-score not mapped to the review step');
+  assert.match(app, /if \(!hash \|\| hash\.startsWith\('#cfg='\)\) return;/,
+    'deep-link handler must not clobber the #cfg= share-link path');
+});


diff --git a/docs/AUDIT-2026-07-26.md b/docs/AUDIT-2026-07-26.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65d60d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/AUDIT-2026-07-26.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Audit — 2026-07-26
+
+A full read-only audit of `brevityA/Core-Builds` (at `main`, commit `0ddab46`) and the
+live site `brevitya.github.io/Core-Builds`, followed by fixes shipped as PRs. This file
+is the durable record: what was found, why, and which PR resolves each item, so the
+rationale travels with the code.
+
+**Versions audited:** Template Suite `3.3.2` · Configurator `2.84.0` · min AIOStreams `2.31.1`
+**After fixes:** Configurator `2.85` · Suite `3.4.0` (on the feature chain)
+
+## Methodology
+- Cloned the repo and ran the full local gauntlet: `node --test` (29), `pytest` (233),
+  `node scripts/validate.mjs` (25), `validate_templates.py` (fleet), and a from-source
+  rebuild of `configurator/index.html` (byte-identical to the committed build).
+- Static analysis of `configurator/src/js/app.js` (6,260 lines) + data modules, the
+  Cloudflare worker, the tools, and every workflow under `.github/workflows/`.
+- Git archaeology on regressions (`git show`/diffs across PRs #554 / #557 / #577).
+- Cross-checked `ROADMAP.md` vs `docs/roadmap.mdx` vs `CHANGELOG.md` vs
+  `docs/changelog.mdx` vs `configurator/.../changelog.js` vs `versions.json` vs the live site.
+- Competitive scan: Tam-Taro, TVFlix, Duck Tools/QuackStart, CrispyDuck, AIOStreams upstream.
+
+The baseline was green (all suites pass). Every finding below was reproduced; every fix
+is covered by a new test (regression test, golden snapshot, or e2e assertion).
+
+## Findings → PR map
+
+| # | Sev | Finding | Root cause | Fix / PR |
+|---|-----|---------|------------|----------|
+| 1 | 🔴 | **Jackett & Prowlarr presets never generated** (production) | `presets()` filter `credKey && apiUrl` never matches Jackett/Prowlarr (no `apiUrl`); the `#557` fix was lost in the v2.84 modular rewrite | Restored `credKey && !apiUrl` + branch-coverage test → `patches/Core-Builds-PR-mixed-tier.patch` (chain #1) |
+| 2 | 🟠 | `validate_templates.py` **crashes when run bare** (`AttributeError` on `Filtering/*.json`) | No guard for non-`dict` roots; default `--dir .` globs expression libraries | Skip non-dict roots gracefully → same patch (chain #1) |
+| 3 | 🟠 | NC-17 "No Restriction" label in Kids Mode reads backwards | Ceiling-semantics value labelled like the strictest option | Noted; left for a UX pass (low risk) — see Open items | same patch (chain #1) documents; UI tweak deferred |
+| 4 | 🟡 | Roadmap is **stale & contradictory** in 4 places | No single source of truth; removed features (Audio Pinnacle / HDR-DV PSE) still listed "Planned" | See "Roadmap" below → `patches/Core-Builds-PR-docs-auto-sync.patch` (independent) |
+| 5 | 🟡 | Unescaped `S.instanceUrl` at `app.js` (~line 1470) | One field missed the `escH` discipline added in the v2.84 security audit | Noted (self-XSS via own input/localStorage); low — fix with `escH` (open item) |
+| 6 | ⚪ | `randomId()` modulo bias in the worker; non-atomic KV counters; legacy dup counter worker | Known roadmap items | Tracked (not blocking) |
+| 7 | ⚪ | `configurator/src/js/patches/` is **dead design-note code** (duplicate fn names, never imported) | Leftover from feature design | Noted for cleanup (open item) |
+| 8 | 🔗 | **41/48 templates live-sync Vidhin05 `@main`** (ranked regex + expressions); elfhosted validates regex by exact string equality | Upstream pushes silently re-rank every user; prior drift caused "X/183 regexes not allowed" | Pinned snapshots + daily drift-watch + tracking issue → `patches/Core-Builds-PR-drift-watch.patch` (independent) |
+| 9 | 🧪 | No guard against generated-template drift | No snapshots of full output | Golden config snapshots (12 combos × 2 viewports) → `patches/Core-Builds-PR-golden-snapshots.patch` (chain #4) |
+| 10 | 🐞 | **Import Custom Formatter opens behind the Fine-Tune drawer** | `.modal-overlay` z-index `200` < drawer `10030` | Dedicated `.above-drawer` (10035) — above drawer, below `#pwdPrompt`@10040 → `patches/Core-Builds-PR-layering-fix.patch` (independent) |
+| 11 | 🐞 | **Stream Availability / Match Aggressiveness help cards clipped** mid-sentence | `.ft-popup` `position:absolute` under the drawer's `overflow-y:auto`; old handler only flipped horizontally | Portal popup to `<body>` `position:fixed` with vertical flip + internal scroll; fixes all 12 tooltips + adds keyboard support → same layering patch |
+| 12 | 🐞 | **Feedback / contact widget missing entirely** | v2.83 module `contact-widget.js` shipped but was never imported/called by `app.js` (wiring lost in the v2.84 rewrite) | Import + `initContactWidget()` in bootstrap + idempotency guard → same layering patch |
+| 13 |  | **Docs frozen** (`changelog.mdx` at v2.9.7, `whats-new.mdx` at v2.78, roadmap "Shipped" stale) | Nothing bridged the two changelogs (root `CHANGELOG.md` = suite log; `changelog.js` = configurator log) into the Mintlify pages | Auto-regenerate the three pages + CI anti-freeze guard + auto Discord announce → `patches/Core-Builds-PR-docs-auto-sync.patch` (independent) |
+| 14 | ✨ | (feature) Mixed / Adaptive resolution tier + Apex-Mixed hybrid | Requested during the audit | `patches/Core-Builds-PR-mixed-tier.patch` (#1), `...-apex-mixed.patch` (#2), `...-apex-mixed-configurator.patch` (#3) |
+
+Severity legend: 🔴 production/data-loss-class · 🟠 breaks a documented workflow · 🟡 correctness/UX · ⚪ hygiene · 🔗 supply-chain · 🧪 test-gap · 🐞 user-reported bug · 🧊 staleness · ✨ feature.
+
+## Roadmap review
+Four records of "done/next" disagreed. Concretely: `ROADMAP.md` listed as *Planned* items
+that had shipped (and two that shipped-then-removed in 3.2.8); `docs/changelog.mdx` was a
+month behind the root changelog; `docs/whats-new.mdx` and the roadmap "Shipped" table were
+hand-maintained and stopped being updated. The docs-auto-sync PR makes the *index* parts of
+these pages regenerate from source (curated prose stays hand-edited inside
+`<!-- AUTO:* -->` managed regions) and adds `tests/test_docs_generated.py`, which re-derives
+each generated page and **fails CI if a committed page has drifted** — so the freeze cannot
+recur silently (verified with a negative control).
+
+## The two changelogs are independent tracks
+The root `CHANGELOG.md` versions the **template suite** (now `3.x`); `changelog.js` versions
+the **configurator** (`2.x`). The freeze happened because nothing mapped either into the
+docs site. Going forward: suite releases flow through `sync-docs.yml` (which now also
+announces to Discord); configurator releases flow through the regenerated `whats-new.mdx`.
+
+## Test totals (before → after, across the chain)
+- Node unit: 29 → 47 (`optional-scrapers`, `resolution-mixed`, `apex-mixed`)
+- Static checks: 25 → 26 (`e2e golden generation hook`)
+- pytest: 233 → 237 (`test_docs_generated`)
+- Playwright e2e: +`ui-fixes` (3: import-modal layering, tooltip portal, feedback widget) + `golden-configs` (12 combos × desktop+mobile)
+
+> Note: `stability.spec.mjs` shows 3 failures **only in this audit's sandbox** — a headless
+> `pageerror`/console-noise quirk that trips `expect(errors).toEqual([])`. Confirmed
+> identical on a clean `main` checkout; passes on real CI runners. Not a product regression.
+
+## Competitive notes (what others do better)
+- **Tam-Taro**: one canonical template + in-wizard customization = far less choice paralysis
+  than our 41 active templates. Our own "tighter 6-template lineup" idea is the right call.
+- **CrispyDuck**: drag-and-drop formatter builder with live preview — our biggest visible
+  feature gap (we have 19 preset formatter strings + a gallery, but no live preview).
+- **Where we lead**: automated validation, host-compatibility matrix, live instance status,
+  diagnostics, device-specific capability profiles, and now golden-snapshot + drift-watch CI.
+  The remaining gap is product surface, not engineering depth.
+
+## Open / product-level items (not in these PRs)
+- Template consolidation decision (6-template lineup) — biggest competitive lever.
+- Formatter live preview (CrispyDuck parity) — foundations exist in the Inspector + gallery.
+- NC-17 label fix; `escH` on `instanceUrl`; delete `configurator/src/js/patches/` dead code.
+- Docs auto-sync: optionally point the synced-release ping at `DISCORD_DOCS_WEBHOOK_URL`
+  instead of `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` (one-line change in `sync-docs.yml`).
+- Docs: add a Mintlify `template-directory.mdx` row for `core-nexus-mixed` (fleet validator
+  and the Torbox README already cover it).
+
+## How the fixes ship
+Seven patches in `patches/` (see `CODESPACES-HOWTO.md` and `push-and-open-prs.sh`):
+
+```
+main
+ ├─ audit/mixed-tier-jackett-fix          (1)
+ │   └─ feature/4k-apex-mixed             (2 <- 1)
+ │       └─ feature/apex-mixed-configurator (3 <- 2)
+ │           └─ feature/golden-config-snapshots (4 <- 3)
+ ├─ ci/vidhin05-drift-watch               (independent)
+ ├─ fix/configurator-layering             (independent)
+ └─ feature/docs-auto-sync                (independent)
+```
+
+Merge the three independents in any order; merge the chain strictly **1 → 2 → 3 → 4**.
+
+---
+*Audit performed against a fresh clone; every suite executed locally; the production
+bundle was rebuilt and inspected for each cited finding.*
-- 
